01:19:53.374 --> 01:19:55.550
- What is your name?
- Prancer: Prancer.

1512
01:19:55.724 --> 01:19:58.902
That's a weird and cool name. I think that name is awesome.

1513
01:19:59.511 --> 01:20:01.034
And yes. I want it known everywhere.

1514
01:20:01.208 --> 01:20:04.516
I want everyone in Napa to know the name "Prancer."

1515
01:20:04.690 --> 01:20:07.519
And I want to rectify all the wrong that's been done

1516
01:20:07.693 --> 01:20:10.348
against me with bullets as hot as the fucking sun. man.

1517
01:20:10.522 --> 01:20:12.132
- [chuckles. sniffles]
- What?

1518
01:20:12.741 --> 01:20:15.092
I want to light this bitch up. I want to kill.

1519
01:20:15.266 --> 01:20:16.615
Hey. hey. hey.

1520
01:20:17.050 --> 01:20:19.836
Hey. don't say stuff like that. That's not fucking cool.

1521
01:20:20.140 --> 01:20:22.403
The last cool thing you could ever do

1522
01:20:22.839 --> 01:20:26.538
is shoot up the fucking school. you incel piece of shit.

1523
01:20:26.973 --> 01:20:28.670
- It's...
- What are you talking about?

1524
01:20:28.845 --> 01:20:30.910
All I'm saying is. "Fuck off. go away. go away. go away."

1525
01:20:30.934 --> 01:20:32.936
Yo. stop. All right? I'm gonna go over there.

1526
01:20:33.110 --> 01:20:34.676
Do you know those kids over there?

1527
01:20:35.677 --> 01:20:37.331
Who really knows anybody. man?

1528
01:20:37.505 --> 01:20:39.725
All right. just get the shit out of your fucking head.

1529
01:20:39.899 --> 01:20:41.442
- Who really knows anybody. man?
- Jack Jr.: All right.

1530
01:20:41.466 --> 01:20:44.208
Very funny. Stop that shit.

1531
01:20:48.299 --> 01:20:51.084
[uplifting music playing]

1532
01:20:51.258 --> 01:20:52.956
- Hey!
- [sighs]

1533
01:20:53.130 --> 01:20:55.306
What's wrong. little friend?

1534
01:20:56.002 --> 01:20:59.005
- Mind if I have a little sit?
- Whatever.

1535
01:20:59.179 --> 01:21:01.747
Well. listen. don't be so sad. What's your little name?

1536
01:21:02.052 --> 01:21:04.793
- Prancer.
- Prancer?

1537
01:21:04.968 --> 01:21:06.273
Prancer: Yeah.

1538
01:21:06.447 --> 01:21:08.536
- Prancer?
- Prancer: [chuckling] Yeah.

1539
01:21:08.710 --> 01:21:11.757
Prancer. the Sitting Bridge Troll.

1540
01:21:12.192 --> 01:21:14.934
- [laughs. sighs]
- Yeah. [Laughs]

1541
01:21:15.108 --> 01:21:17.415
God. you really changed my mind about things.

1542
01:21:17.589 --> 01:21:19.591
- Miles Jr.?
- Oh. my...

1543
01:21:19.765 --> 01:21:21.810
I think you're going to want to follow me.

1544
01:21:25.336 --> 01:21:28.165
- Come on.
- Um. just promise me. okay?

1545
01:21:28.339 --> 01:21:29.470
I will.

1546
01:21:29.644 --> 01:21:30.964
Follow your dream no matter what.

1547
01:21:32.865 --> 01:21:35.172
Jack Jr.: Guys. something's happening to the amulet.

1548
01:21:35.346 --> 01:21:39.437
- [echoes] Is it a portal?
- [grandiose music playing]

1549
01:21:41.613 --> 01:21:43.963
- Puck: Where are we?
- Portal?

1550
01:21:44.137 --> 01:21:46.009
- [eagle screeches]
- [all gasp]

1551
01:21:46.183 --> 01:21:49.447
- Are we in space?
- Come on now. buddy.

1552
01:21:49.751 --> 01:21:50.927
I may have brain damage.

1553
01:21:51.101 --> 01:21:52.295
but even I know if we were in space.

1554
01:21:52.319 --> 01:21:53.320
we couldn't breathe.

1555
01:21:53.494 --> 01:21:54.974
Look. this way.

1556
01:22:01.285 --> 01:22:04.941
[dramatic music playing]

1557
01:22:05.115 --> 01:22:07.030
Group: The Sommelier.

1558
01:22:07.204 --> 01:22:08.988
Napa Boy rule number eleven.

1559
01:22:09.162 --> 01:22:11.382
"Always believe in The Sommelier."

1560
01:22:11.730 --> 01:22:13.514
I believe you have something of mine.

1561
01:22:13.688 --> 01:22:14.820
Oh! [Chuckles]

1562
01:22:15.342 --> 01:22:17.475
[breathes heavily]

1563
01:22:18.041 --> 01:22:20.304
Here. Here. Mr. Sommelier.

1564
01:22:22.262 --> 01:22:25.657
Glad you received my amulet's call. Miss Puck.

1565
01:22:26.266 --> 01:22:28.486
- Miles Jr.: My intern?
- Jack Jr.: See. Miles Jr.?

1566
01:22:28.660 --> 01:22:30.836
The Sommelier had a plan all along.

1567
01:22:31.010 --> 01:22:32.751
This all happened so Puck could discover

1568
01:22:32.925 --> 01:22:35.058
the only good Merlot to ever exist.

1569
01:22:36.059 --> 01:22:37.408
Nice job. Puck.

1570
01:22:37.582 --> 01:22:39.142
- [group applauds]
- [Jack Jr. chuckles]

1571
01:22:39.192 --> 01:22:40.604
- Miles Jr.: Yeah.
- Mitch: Way to go. Puck.

1572
01:22:40.628 --> 01:22:42.065
Why. Sommelier?

1573
01:22:42.239 --> 01:22:44.763
Why have you asked us to come all this way?

1574
01:22:44.937 --> 01:22:47.200
Jack Jr.. care to explain?

1575
01:22:47.679 --> 01:22:50.247
- Yeah.
- J... Jack Jr.?

1576
01:22:50.464 --> 01:22:55.426
- [gentle music playing]
- Oh. my God. What the fuck?

1577
01:22:55.600 --> 01:22:57.186
Jack Jr.: I just wanted the Napa Boys to go

1578
01:22:57.210 --> 01:22:58.516
on one last adventure.

1579
01:22:58.690 --> 01:23:00.648
That's right. Jack Jr. hired me.

1580
01:23:01.780 --> 01:23:03.738
I've been working on his last will and testament

1581
01:23:03.912 --> 01:23:06.437
- this entire time.
- Thanks. man. [Chuckles]

1582
01:23:06.611 --> 01:23:10.615
Yes. that's why Jack Jr. hired Stifler's brother.

1583
01:23:11.050 --> 01:23:12.690
We love you. buddy. We love you the most.

1584
01:23:12.834 --> 01:23:14.575
I know you love me the most.

1585
01:23:14.749 --> 01:23:17.839
All of these things are things that I knew and planned for.

1586
01:23:18.275 --> 01:23:20.625
Jack Jr. versus the Big C.

1587
01:23:21.147 --> 01:23:23.236
I bet that's gonna make a great comic book.

1588
01:23:23.410 --> 01:23:25.499
I... I...

1589
01:23:25.891 --> 01:23:28.589
[sobbing] I don't know. It's just so funny

1590
01:23:28.763 --> 01:23:30.678
that you mentioned cancer tonight.

1591
01:23:31.723 --> 01:23:33.986
"Funny"? Please explain.

1592
01:23:34.160 --> 01:23:37.207
Okay. I was talking to this New Class kid.

1593
01:23:37.381 --> 01:23:40.688
and she had cancer of the dream.

1594
01:23:41.037 --> 01:23:42.560
Because she kept saying.

1595
01:23:42.734 --> 01:23:44.614
"I... I'm not going to live my ultimate dream."

1596
01:23:44.779 --> 01:23:45.930
and I said. "Always follow your dream

1597
01:23:45.954 --> 01:23:47.086
no matter what."

1598
01:23:48.131 --> 01:23:49.567
Was her name Prancer?

1599
01:23:49.741 --> 01:23:52.570
"Prancer?" "Uh. hi. Santa. um..."

1600
01:23:53.484 --> 01:23:55.486
[exhales sharply] "Santa. get the..."

1601
01:23:57.096 --> 01:23:58.750
I... I think her name was Prancer.

1602
01:23:59.272 --> 01:24:02.406
♪ ["You Can't Hurry Love" by The Supremes playing] ♪

1603
01:24:02.580 --> 01:24:04.016
[car horn honking]

1604
01:24:04.669 --> 01:24:06.975
Miles Jr.. you really fucked up this time.

1605
01:24:07.150 --> 01:24:09.230
- Miles Jr.: No. right.
- Jack Jr.: I am going right.

1606
01:24:09.282 --> 01:24:10.642
Puck: Why did you tell the shooter

1607
01:24:10.718 --> 01:24:12.198
to follow their dream?

1608
01:24:12.372 --> 01:24:13.567
Miles Jr.: Because I didn't know it was a shooter!

1609
01:24:13.591 --> 01:24:15.114
Puck: Hey!

1610
01:24:15.288 --> 01:24:16.918
Stifler's brother: You're going the wrong way. Jack Jr.

1611
01:24:16.942 --> 01:24:18.742
Jack Jr.: Will you please talk one at a time.

1612
01:24:18.857 --> 01:24:21.033
- Puck: You missed the turn!
- Jack Jr.: What?

1613
01:24:21.207 --> 01:24:24.732
- [all scream]
- [tires screeching]

1614
01:24:24.906 --> 01:24:26.623
Stifler's brother: The reason we're in this mess

1615
01:24:26.647 --> 01:24:28.364
- is you. Miles Jr.
- Miles Jr.: That is not true!

1616
01:24:28.388 --> 01:24:30.588
Jack Jr.: Look. we can all agree it's Miles Jr.'s fault

1617
01:24:30.651 --> 01:24:32.392
that Napa High is going to get shot up.

1618
01:24:32.566 --> 01:24:35.395
but now I need answers. Where is Napa High?

1619
01:24:35.787 --> 01:24:37.441
[group screams]

1620
01:24:37.615 --> 01:24:39.375
Stop. stop! I can see her! Right there! Right there!

1621
01:24:39.399 --> 01:24:42.315
Jack Jr.: Go. go. go! Miles Jr.. go. go!

1622
01:24:42.620 --> 01:24:44.143
[whimpers] Don't shoot!

1623
01:24:44.317 --> 01:24:47.059
- [Jack Jr. pants]
- Puck: Miles Jr.!

1624
01:24:47.233 --> 01:24:48.887
- Mitch: Wait! [Pants]
- Puck: Over here!

1625
01:24:49.061 --> 01:24:52.586
No! No! No. there it is! There's the shooter!

1626
01:24:53.109 --> 01:24:54.414
Jack Jr.: Fuck. we're too late!

1627
01:24:54.893 --> 01:24:57.069
Miles Jr.: Don't shoot her! She's gonna shoot 'em!

1628
01:24:57.243 --> 01:24:59.083
Stifler's brother: Don't shoot up your school!

1629
01:24:59.724 --> 01:25:03.467
[menacing music playing]

1630
01:25:08.950 --> 01:25:10.865
- [music concludes]
- Wait! That's the moose!

1631
01:25:12.215 --> 01:25:13.215
Oh.

1632
01:25:16.958 --> 01:25:18.786
That's no moose.

1633
01:25:19.439 --> 01:25:22.181
- Yes. it is. It's a moose.
- Oh. yes. It is. it is.

1634
01:25:22.355 --> 01:25:24.749
- [grunts]
- [pants]

1635
01:25:27.578 --> 01:25:29.493
- [moose grunting]
- [Prancer screaming]

1636
01:25:30.407 --> 01:25:32.757
- Oh.
- Damn. Get her.

1637
01:25:33.453 --> 01:25:35.733
- Get her. moose. Get her. Yeah.
- Stifler's brother: Ooh.

1638
01:25:35.803 --> 01:25:38.893
Now that's some good old-fashioned Napa Boy karma.

1639
01:25:39.067 --> 01:25:40.330
Eh. Puck?

1640
01:25:40.895 --> 01:25:42.636
Aye. As The Merchant of Venice taught us.

1641
01:25:42.810 --> 01:25:43.810
the truth will out.

1642
01:25:43.942 --> 01:25:45.726
Don't shoot up your school.

1643
01:25:46.205 --> 01:25:48.729
If there's anything that ruins the vibe in America.

1644
01:25:48.903 --> 01:25:50.078
it's a school shooting.

1645
01:25:50.992 --> 01:25:53.430
That moose is slow dancing with that troubled youth.

1646
01:25:53.604 --> 01:25:55.693
- [moose grunting]
- Is that a waltz?

1647
01:25:55.867 --> 01:25:57.912
I never thought I'd live to solve the mystery

1648
01:25:58.086 --> 01:25:59.392
of whether a moose can waltz.

1649
01:26:00.654 --> 01:26:04.310
Hey. speaking of mysteries. we never did solve the mystery

1650
01:26:04.484 --> 01:26:06.660
of who wrote F-slur on my winery barrels.

1651
01:26:08.532 --> 01:26:11.143
- I'll admit it. I did.
- [chuckles]

1652
01:26:12.275 --> 01:26:14.277
Wait. I did too.

1653
01:26:14.451 --> 01:26:16.888
- What?
- I did too.

1654
01:26:17.149 --> 01:26:19.717
- [chuckles] Stifler's brother?
- Miles Jr.: We all did.

1655
01:26:19.891 --> 01:26:23.286
We all wrote it so we could bond together

1656
01:26:23.460 --> 01:26:25.113
and bond through tragedy

1657
01:26:25.288 --> 01:26:28.639
because we're the Napa Boys of friendship.

1658
01:26:28.813 --> 01:26:32.599
I mean. I guess it worked. It really did work.

1659
01:26:33.209 --> 01:26:36.081
I did too. but I meant it.

1660
01:26:36.473 --> 01:26:38.344
Group: Squirm!

1661
01:26:38.518 --> 01:26:40.607
I always wanted to be one of you Napa Boys.

1662
01:26:41.391 --> 01:26:43.349
- Really?
- Yeah. right.

1663
01:26:43.523 --> 01:26:45.264
- [Stifler's brother grunting]
- [grunts]

1664
01:26:45.438 --> 01:26:47.135
My favorite shirt!

1665
01:26:47.397 --> 01:26:49.660
[group laughing]

1666
01:26:52.271 --> 01:26:56.623
[cheering]

1667
01:26:58.146 --> 01:26:59.974
Oh. also. Kim's not my daughter.

1668
01:27:00.148 --> 01:27:01.498
- So. hey!
- Hey!

1669
01:27:01.672 --> 01:27:04.327
Jack Jr.: Yeah. isn't that good? It's good. yeah.

1670
01:27:04.501 --> 01:27:06.503
But me and Monica are adopting her.

1671
01:27:06.677 --> 01:27:07.917
Mitch: Hey. that's really nice.

1672
01:27:08.069 --> 01:27:09.157
Yeah. that's great.

1673
01:27:09.332 --> 01:27:10.637
To adventure.

1674
01:27:10.811 --> 01:27:12.552
To the adventure and to the Napa Boys.

1675
01:27:13.205 --> 01:27:15.294
[triumphant music playing]

1676
01:27:17.035 --> 01:27:18.166
Jack Jr.: Now he's Zorro.

1677
01:27:18.341 --> 01:27:20.081
[all laughing]

1678
01:27:26.262 --> 01:27:28.196
Jack Jr.: I'm never going to forget this adventure.

1679
01:27:28.220 --> 01:27:29.620
It's probably my favorite adventure

1680
01:27:29.787 --> 01:27:31.658
- out of all of them.
- [group chuckles]

1681
01:27:40.014 --> 01:27:42.626
[all laugh]

1682
01:27:51.025 --> 01:27:53.114
Jack Jr.: This is the best adventure!

1683
01:27:55.247 --> 01:27:56.683
Whoo!

1684
01:28:03.299 --> 01:28:05.344
Group: To Trixie! To Trixie!

1685
01:28:44.165 --> 01:28:46.167
[music concludes]

1686
01:28:48.344 --> 01:28:50.346
[gentle music playing]

1687
01:31:36.599 --> 01:31:38.514
[music concludes]
